coordination patterns (how agents communicate), but there are several others commonly used in Agentic AI frameworks 
like AutoGen, CrewAI, LangGraph, and Microsoft Agent Framework.


Here's a complete overview.

| Pattern                       | Description                                                                      | Best Use Case                   |
| ----------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |
| **Sequential**                | Agents execute one after another in a fixed order.                               | Data processing, workflows      |
| **Parallel**                  | Multiple agents work simultaneously and their results are combined.              | Search, analysis, summarization |
| **Group Chat**                | Multiple agents communicate together in a shared conversation.                   | Brainstorming, discussions      |
| **Hierarchical**              | A manager/supervisor agent assigns work to worker agents.                        | Enterprise workflows            |
| **Round Robin**               | Each agent takes turns speaking in sequence.                                     | Reviews, brainstorming          |
| **Router (Intent-Based)**     | A router agent decides which specialist agent should handle the request.         | Customer support, help desks    |
| **Planner–Executor**          | One agent creates a plan, another executes it.                                   | Task automation                 |
| **Planner–Executor–Reviewer** | Planner creates a plan, executor performs it, reviewer validates it.             | Coding, document writing        |
| **Critic Pattern**            | One agent performs the task, another critiques and improves the output.          | Writing, code review            |
| **Debate Pattern**            | Multiple agents argue different viewpoints before reaching a conclusion.         | Decision making, research       |
| **Reflection Pattern**        | The same or another agent reviews and improves its own answer.                   | Higher-quality reasoning        |
| **Human-in-the-Loop**         | A human approves or edits before continuing.                                     | Medical, legal, finance         |
| **Event-Driven**              | Agents respond when specific events occur.                                       | Monitoring, alerts              |
| **Swarm**                     | Many agents work independently toward the same goal without a strict hierarchy.  | Large-scale distributed tasks   |
| **Blackboard**                | Agents share information through a common workspace instead of talking directly. | Complex collaborative systems   |


